ADR 0022 lines 57-60 have been wrong since k338 and still are after k348. They say corefile_host_address "reads the mapping regardless of which block the line sits in". Since k338 the record is read from the server block that answers the name.

Replacement text proposed by the k348 worker (amend in place or supersede: the adr-auditor decides, by the repo convention):
> The writer and the probe read `registry.local` from the server block CoreDNS answers it from (k338), including the `*.server` snippets a k3s Corefile imports from `coredns-custom` (k348). A snippet that maps it to the control plane counts as solved; one that maps it elsewhere is `spec` drift that `ocp apply` does not close, and the writer warns rather than writing a record that would be shadowed. OCP still does not write or maintain the snippet. Only plain-DNS server blocks on port 53 count as answering. `*.override` imports are deliberately not read.

Also: .claude/skills/ocp-registry/SKILL.md and README.md say nothing about coredns-custom being read (ocp-doc-writer). Lanes: ocp-adr-auditor (ADR), ocp-doc-writer (skill + README).

